  "summary": "Bold warp-ikat and supplementary-wrap cloths of Timor — the national dress of independence.",
  "description": "Tais are the handwoven textiles of Timor: thick cotton bands in flame reds and blacks, patterned by warp ikat with ancestral figures, and by buna'en supplementary-wrapping that beads geometric motifs across the stripes. Woven on backstrap looms by women for mortuary rites, marriage exchange and ceremonial dress, tais became the flag-like emblem of East Timorese identity through the resistance years and now leads national ceremonies. Manufaha and Liksá styles carry region-specific codes of clan and place.",
